Sval: closing a reopened tab returns to the tab it was reopened over

undoCloseTab opens the closed tab with addTrustedTab, whose inBackground
defaults to true, so the tab gets no owner, and then selects it. Every
other tab opened in front of the selected one has that tab as its owner
(addTab's ownerTab default), so closing it returns there. Closing a
reopened tab instead selected whichever visible tab sat next to it.

diff --git a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
index 6b9691b1ea..a6820f09fa 100644
--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
@@ -4683,6 +4683,8 @@ var SessionStoreInternal = {
     let tab = (tabbrowser.selectedTab = tabbrowser.addTrustedTab(null, {
       // Append the tab if we're opening into a different window,
       tabIndex: aSource == aTargetWindow ? pos : Infinity,
+      // It opens in front of the selected tab, so closing it goes back there.
+      ownerTab: tabbrowser.selectedTab,
       pinned: state.pinned,
       userContextId: state.userContextId,
       skipLoad: true,
